================================================================================
Origin and acknowledgement
================================================================================

andes has its own peptide-spectrum scoring, its own statistical models trained
on public PRIDE data, and an independent Rust implementation.

andes began as a fork of MS-GF+ (Kim & Pevzner, Nat Commun 2014;5:5277) — its
origin; see HERITAGE.md for the lineage. Its design also draws on ideas from the
broader open-source proteomics search-engine community, and we gratefully
acknowledge:

  - X!Tandem  (Craig & Beavis, Bioinformatics 2004)
  - Comet     (Eng, Jahan & Hoopmann, Proteomics 2013)
  - Sage      (Lazear, J. Proteome Res. 2023)
